        "note_tweet": {
          "entities": {},
          "text": "Today, Linux celebrates its 35th anniversary and the remarkable journey of one of the most influential technologies in computing history.\n\nIn 1991, a young Finnish developer named Linus Torvalds purchased his first PC, powered by an Intel 386 processor. After spending time learning x86 assembly language, Linus shared publicly that he was developing a free operating system as a hobby, marking the beginning of Linux.\n\nThe history of Intel and Linux runs deep, and we've had the privilege of watching it grow from a humble passion project into the world's largest open-source OS. Together with the Linux community, we've helped drive innovation across everything from PCs and data centers to cloud, edge, and AI."
        },
